.SH SCAN TECHNIQUES
.PP
One TCP scan type can run at a time.
It can be combined with \f[V]-sU\f[R], one of
\f[V]-sY\f[R]/\f[V]-sZ\f[R], \f[V]-sO\f[R], \f[V]-sV\f[R] and
\f[V]-sC\f[R] in a single run, for example \f[V]-sS -sU -sV\f[R].
As in nmap, the letters can be run together after one \f[V]-s\f[R]:
\f[V]-sCV\f[R] is \f[V]-sC -sV\f[R], and \f[V]-sSU\f[R] is
\f[V]-sS -sU\f[R].
.PP
With no \f[V]-s\f[R] option, FeroProbe runs a SYN scan when it may use
raw sockets (root or \f[V]CAP_NET_RAW\f[R] on Linux) and a connect scan
otherwise, as nmap does.
It also falls back to a connect scan when an IPv6 target is given on a
system without IPv6 raw sockets.
An explicit scan type (\f[V]-sU\f[R], \f[V]-sY\f[R], \f[V]-sZ\f[R],
\f[V]-sO\f[R]) runs on its own and does not add the default TCP scan;
\f[V]-sV\f[R] alone keeps it.
.PP
The raw-socket scans need Linux with root or \f[V]CAP_NET_RAW\f[R]; see
Privileges and platforms.
All scan types support IPv4 and IPv6.
.PP
Like nmap\[aq]s, the probes of the raw-socket scans, of host discovery
and of the UDP scan go out without the \[dq]don\[aq]t fragment\[dq] bit
and with a random TTL (IPv6: hop limit) from 37 to 59, picked again for
every probe.
Traceroute sets its own TTLs.
.SS TCP SYN scan (\f[V]-sS\f[R])
.PP
Sends a SYN and reads the answer without completing the handshake: a
SYN-ACK means \f[V]open\f[R], a reset \f[V]closed\f[R], and no answer or
an ICMP unreachable error \f[V]filtered\f[R].
Unanswered probes are resent as the host\[aq]s losses call for, up to
\f[V]--retries\f[R] times (see Resends and delays).
This is the default scan as root.
.SS TCP connect scan (\f[V]-sT\f[R])
.PP
Asks the operating system to connect to each port, so it needs no
privileges and works on Linux, macOS and Windows.
A completed connection means \f[V]open\f[R], a refused one
\f[V]closed\f[R], and a timeout \f[V]filtered\f[R].
An open port\[aq]s connection is closed at once with a reset, as nmap
does, rather than with a FIN.
This is the default scan without raw sockets.
It carries no FeroProbe signature, since it is an ordinary connection.
On Windows, a refused connection is reported only about 2 seconds after
the reset arrives, so there a connect try never waits less than 3 s,
whatever the timeout options say.
.SS FIN, NULL, Xmas and Maimon scans (\f[V]-sF\f[R], \f[V]-sN\f[R], \f[V]-sX\f[R], \f[V]-sM\f[R])
.PP
.TS
