.TE
.PP
A probe with no payload, like \f[V]null\f[R], connects and listens.
The built-in parsers for binary replies (SQL Server, SMB, RDP, LDAP,
DNS, NTP, SNMP, SSDP and NetBIOS) run on the replies to the probes of
those names.
.PP
\f[V]match SERVICE REGEX\f[R] and \f[V]softmatch SERVICE REGEX\f[R]
define a rule.
The regular expression is the rest of the line, run on the raw reply
with \f[V].\f[R] matching any byte, newlines included, and
\f[V]\[rs]xNN\f[R] matching byte \f[V]NN\f[R] (Rust regex syntax, flags
\f[V](?s-u)\f[R]); write \f[V]\[rs]x20\f[R] for a space at either end.
Rules are tried in file order, hard matches before soft ones, and the
first match wins.
A soft match takes only \f[V]probe\f[R].
