.TE
.PP
At least one rule and \f[V]action\f[R] are required.
Rules cannot use sockets.
While a script runs, \f[V]SCRIPT_NAME\f[R] holds its name and
\f[V]SCRIPT_TYPE\f[R] the rule it runs under
(\f[V]\[dq]prerule\[dq]\f[R], \f[V]\[dq]hostrule\[dq]\f[R],
\f[V]\[dq]portrule\[dq]\f[R], \f[V]\[dq]postrule\[dq]\f[R]).
.PP
\f[B]The host table:\f[R] \f[V]ip\f[R] (the address as text),
\f[V]name\f[R] (its reverse DNS name, or \f[V]\[dq]\[dq]\f[R]),
\f[V]targetname\f[R] (the name given on the command line, if any),
\f[V]mac_addr\f[R] (if known) and \f[V]os\f[R] (the names of the OS
matches, best first, with \f[V]-O\f[R]).
.PP
\f[B]The port table:\f[R] \f[V]number\f[R], \f[V]protocol\f[R]
(\f[V]\[dq]tcp\[dq]\f[R], \f[V]\[dq]udp\[dq]\f[R], ...), \f[V]state\f[R]
(\f[V]\[dq]open\[dq]\f[R], ...), \f[V]reason\f[R], \f[V]service\f[R]
(the service name) and \f[V]version\f[R], a table with \f[V]name\f[R],
\f[V]product\f[R], \f[V]version\f[R], \f[V]extrainfo\f[R],
\f[V]hostname\f[R], \f[V]ostype\f[R], \f[V]devicetype\f[R],
\f[V]service_tunnel\f[R] (\f[V]\[dq]ssl\[dq]\f[R] or
\f[V]\[dq]none\[dq]\f[R]) and \f[V]cpe\f[R] (a list), as far as
\f[V]-sV\f[R] found them.
.PP
